  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Peggy-O** (1 review): Reviewer singles out Peggy-O as a nice version [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **gd1979-02-06.169936.aud.tulsa.LaFortune.miller.flac1644** (recommended): audience recording; 20 songs; 161 min; rated 4.25/5 by 4 [1]. Said about its sound: The tape has various cuts; the uploader cleaned them up, but it remains imperfect, though better than the version received; Donna is very hard to hear in parts of the recording; A genuine audience recording that puts the listener among the fans [1][2][4][5]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- A Johnny B. Goode encore is missing from the tape; New Minglewood Blues and Stagger Lee may also have been played [1]\n- Reviewer calls this the last missing show from the post-hiatus era, one of three lost shows recently found [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **gd1979-02-06.169936.aud.tulsa.LaFortune.miller.flac1644**: taped by Bill LaFortune; transferred by Transfer by John LaFortune Mastering by Charlie Miller  January 28, 2025; source: Shure Mics > Cassette Master (Nakamichi 550) > Cassette (Maxell XL-IIS) [1]. Also: Files came from John LaFortune; the microphones were taped to chair legs so they stayed hidden; Charlie Miller cleaned up the recording, which the reviewer says was made by the mayor of Tulsa [1][2]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Fan art by lostlivedead.blogspot.com: [February 6, 1979 The Pavilion, Tulsa, OK: Grateful Dead (Last Lost Live Tape)](https://lostlivedead.blogspot.com/2020/08/february-6-1979-pavilion-tulsa-ok.html) [7]\n- Poster by Jerry Garcia: [1979-02-06 Backstage Pass - Jerry Garcia](https://jerrygarcia.com/image/1979-02-06-backstage-pass/) [8]\n- Poster by pleasantdeadposter.com: [Grateful Dead Tulsa 1979 poster RARE/LIMITED Signed by Carl Barger](https://pleasantdeadposter.com/grateful-dead-tulsa-1979-poster-rare-limited-signed-by-carl-barger.htm) [9]",
